    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38018" root="لهب" body-key="l">
    
      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تلهّبت النَّارُ</span></b> , quasi-pass. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهَّبَ</span>, (K,) [same
as ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلْتَهَبَتْ</span></b> , except that it has an intensive signification;] <i>The fire flamed,</i> or <i>blazed,</i> (S,) [<i>fiercely,</i>
or <i>intensely,</i> or <i>flamed,</i> or <i>blazed, burned without
smoke, fiercely,</i> or <i>intensely</i>].― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تلهّب جُوعًا</span>, and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جوعا</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">التهب</span></b> , (tropical:)  <i>He burned with hunger.</i> (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تلهّب غَيْظًا</span> <i>He burned,</i> and <i>was</i> or <i>became
hot, with wrath,</i> or <i>rage.</i> (TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وغر</span>.)
See 8.

